  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「カプシクム・キネンセ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AB%E3%83%97%E3%82%B7%E3%82%AF%E3%83%A0%E3%83%BB%E3%82%AD%E3%83%8D%E3%83%B3%E3%82%BB",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107249940,
      "text": "カプシクム・キネンセ は、小型の低木となるトウガラシ属の1種である。ハバネロなどの唐辛子の品種はこの種に属する。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Capsicum chinense」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capsicum_chinense",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1370535889,
      "text": "Capsicum chinense, commonly known as a \"habanero-type pepper\", is a species of chili pepper native to the Americas. C. chinense varieties are well known for their unique flavors and, in many cases, exceptional heat. The hottest peppers in the world are members of this species, with a Scoville heat unit score of 2.69 million measured in the C. chinense cultivar Pepper X in 2023."
    }
  },
